WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:07.109
The world is a dangerous place but, depending
on where you’re from, tha dangers you face

00:00:07.109 --> 00:00:08.820
can be very different.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:14.140
Obviously a kid from war-torn Iraq is going
to be wary of completely different things

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:20.850
to a child from the wilds of Canada; bombs
versus bears, glaring sun versus metres of

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:21.850
snow.

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:26.860
So, please fasten your seatbelt, put on your
hard hat, sit down and take your tablets and

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:34.579
let’s look at just a few of the ways that
the world is trying to kill you.

00:00:34.579 --> 00:00:40.280
With all the talk of driverless cars and Uber,
as well as ingenious safety systems like automatic

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:46.109
breaking, it’s easy to forget that driving
can actually be a pretty dangerous activity.

00:00:46.109 --> 00:00:50.320
So what is the worst place to hop behind the
wheel?

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:57.460
Right now, it’s Iran, with a rate of about
44 per 100,000 people dying each year on the

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:58.460
roads.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:03.760
That’s almost 15 times the rate in the UK,
which is the third safest place to drive in

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:07.270
the world, only beaten by Sweden and Micronesia.

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:12.610
However, countries like Libya and Iraq are
also high on the list of the most dangerous

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:17.350
places to drive, which is understandable since
the instability in those regions means there

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:19.620
is no real policing of the roads.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:23.460
Also, the condition of the tarmac is probably
pretty awful.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:27.500
War has an annoying tendency to make a big
mess of everything.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:35.050
But there is no war in Iran, so what is the
reason behind their dangerous driving?

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:41.920
One main factor is actually the country’s
most popular car; the Kia Pride, made by Saipa.

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:49.990
It accounts for 40% of cars on the road and
is described by police as a “death coach”

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:53.460
and they’ve even asked for its production
to be halted.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:02:00.020
The government has also waded in and one official,
Mohammad Reza Mamdouhi, described it as being

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:04.220
“detrimental to the mental health of those
who are easily agitated”.

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:07.530
As slogans go, I’ve heard better.

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:12.260
BMW - The Ultimate Driving Machine
Jaguar – Born to Perform

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:17.890
The Kia Pride – Putting the mental in detrimental
To be fair, it’s not quite as bad as the

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:21.659
old Volkswagen advert – Relieves Gas Pain.

00:02:21.659 --> 00:02:24.090
Even Iran’s neighbours are scared of The
Pride.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:28.959
Photos of a few dozen new models lined up
at the border prompted one Iraqi journalist

00:02:28.959 --> 00:02:36.019
to joke that the question for Iraqis was “whether
the Pride is more dangerous than Daesh (ISIS)”

00:02:36.019 --> 00:02:41.969
You might be thinking; if it’s so awful,
why does everyone drive it?

00:02:41.969 --> 00:02:47.060
Well that’s largely down to the international
sanctions that have been put on Iran over

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:49.439
its nuclear weapons programme.

00:02:49.439 --> 00:02:51.760
They don’t get a lot of foreign imports.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:57.040
So the new nuclear treaty that has been signed
recently will hopefully open up the trade

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:00.239
of vehicles, much to the relief of the locals.

00:03:00.239 --> 00:03:04.599
I’m pretty sure some of them would have
rather braved nuclear winter, than get in

00:03:04.599 --> 00:03:08.409
the ironically named Pride once again.

00:03:08.409 --> 00:03:13.849
For those people trying to go on a trip without
a car, there is always the chemical option.

00:03:13.849 --> 00:03:16.810
The world takes a lot of drugs.

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:24.510
To give you some idea, so far this year, the
world has spent $120 billion dollars on illegal

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:26.599
substances, and it’s only April.

00:03:26.599 --> 00:03:31.030
What’s more, that doesn’t include the
other billions from prescription drugs, which

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:32.920
are abused constantly.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:38.730
The most drug related deaths per capita are
found in Iceland, which may surprise you,

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:42.780
at a rate of about 21 people per 100,000.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:47.739
A lot of the other northern European countries
are high on the list too, Finland and Estonia

00:03:47.739 --> 00:03:49.069
for example.

00:03:49.069 --> 00:03:53.629
We suspect those long winters, with month
after month of darkness, can really take a

00:03:53.629 --> 00:03:58.019
toll on your mood so it makes sense you might
want a bit of escapism.

00:03:58.019 --> 00:04:05.760
Iceland also has the highest percentage of
marijuana users, with almost 20% of the population

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:08.099
estimated to take it regularly.

00:04:08.099 --> 00:04:14.510
Scotland leads the world for cocaine usage,
at 2.5% of the population, which is maybe

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:18.220
why tourists have such a hard time understanding
what they’re saying.

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:24.379
And, surprisingly, Australia is the world’s
leading user of ecstasy, with about 3% of

00:04:24.379 --> 00:04:26.120
the country taking it.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:30.220
You would have thought permanent sunshine
and beaches would be enough, but apparently

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:31.220
not.

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:35.490
In the US, which is very high on the list
of drug related death nations, the notorious

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:39.500
War on Drugs is generally believed to have
failed.

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:44.599
John Ehrlichman, one of Richard Nixon’s
lead advisors, has admitted that the Comprehensive

00:04:44.599 --> 00:04:50.879
Drug Abuse Prevention and Control Act of 1971,
that was the real start of the war on drugs,

00:04:50.879 --> 00:04:57.031
was really a policy tool to go after anti-war
protesters and black communities, since they

00:04:57.031 --> 00:05:00.449
were the biggest political threat to Nixon
at the time.

00:05:00.449 --> 00:05:04.669
Drug legalisation is beginning to appear around
the world, now that governments can look at

00:05:04.669 --> 00:05:09.389
the data provided by pioneering programs in
countries such as the Netherlands, Portugal

00:05:09.389 --> 00:05:11.250
and Mexico.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:15.509
Cannabis legalisation in the states seems
to be going smoothly and cannabis legal states

00:05:15.509 --> 00:05:23.460
had massive revenues of $5.4 billion in 2015,
and they’re thought to rise again to $6.7

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:24.740
billion this year.

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:30.770
Colorado alone generates over $10 million
in tax a month for its state government.

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:33.370
That’s the power of going green.

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:38.380
But, overdose is not the only way drugs can
damage a country.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:43.099
If you want to see some of its secondary effects
then we need to look at a different death

00:05:43.099 --> 00:05:44.099
rate.

00:05:44.099 --> 00:05:50.080
The Central American country El Salvador is
the murder capital of the world, having overtaken

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:53.039
Honduras in 2015.

00:05:53.039 --> 00:05:59.050
Almost 1 in every 1000 people are killed every
year in El Salvador.

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:04.979
2015 was such a bad year that it’s believed
one person was killed per hour.

00:06:04.979 --> 00:06:13.389
That makes El Salvador 20 times deadlier than
the US and 90 times deadlier than the UK.

00:06:13.389 --> 00:06:18.349
Drugs play a big role since this is what provides
an income for the viscous gangs that terrorise

00:06:18.349 --> 00:06:19.580
the country.

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:25.159
Some drugs, mainly cocaine, pass through from
South America on their way up to Mexico and

00:06:25.159 --> 00:06:26.300
the US.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:30.500
The drugs that are sold in El Salvador are
the cheaper form, crack cocaine.

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:35.180
It also has the world’s highest amphetamine
usage per capita.

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:42.379
El Salvador had a brutal 12 year civil war
from 1980 to 1992 and it left the country

00:06:42.379 --> 00:06:44.000
in tatters.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:48.659
Since that time, two main gangs began to establish
themselves.

00:06:48.659 --> 00:06:56.680
Mara Salvatrucha (MS-13) and Barrio 18; both
gangs actually started out in Los Angeles,

00:06:56.680 --> 00:07:01.819
MS-13 in the 80s and Barrio 18 as early as
the 60s.

00:07:01.819 --> 00:07:07.440
But they both spread down into Central America
and are now the 2 most powerful groups in

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:08.710
El Salvador.

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:14.379
They are both highly organised and have very
strict codes of conduct for their members.

00:07:14.379 --> 00:07:20.440
They often have full body and face tattoos,
with the numbers 13 and 18 featuring heavily,

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:22.259
depending on which side they’re on.

00:07:22.259 --> 00:07:28.340
And like the hazard sign on a bottle of poison,
those marking are a very real warning, they

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:29.580
are brutal.

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:34.410
In August of 2015 the government tried to
enforce yet another crack down on the gangs

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:41.639
and they responded by executing a dozen bus
drivers, just to turn the city into chaos.

00:07:41.639 --> 00:07:48.569
The whole month was a blood bath, with over
900 murders, 52 on just one day.

00:07:48.569 --> 00:07:53.590
Surprisingly, the country still gets almost
1.5 million tourists a year.

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:58.140
A good deal is a good deal, I guess, just
remember to learn your gang greetings, you

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:02.229
never know when they might come in handy,
no pun intended.

00:08:02.229 --> 00:08:06.840
Okay, now if we forget about human killers
for a moment, where do you think you are most

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:10.600
likely to be slain by one of our animal kin?

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:13.080
Let me try and read your mind…I bet most
of you are thinking…

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:14.080
Australia?

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:15.080
Right?

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:16.350
Well, I see why you would think that.

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:21.030
It seems like everything is out to get you;
spiders in your shoes, snakes in your car,

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:26.039
sharks under your surfboard, crocodiles in
your pool, ostriches and kangaroos just generally

00:08:26.039 --> 00:08:28.270
hanging about, looking menacing.

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:34.209
But, although these dangers are real, the
actual death rate is surprisingly low.

00:08:34.209 --> 00:08:38.710
This is probably due to good access to medical
care and a general awareness of how to deal

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:40.500
with these creatures.

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:46.399
Finding the deadliest animal country is actually
pretty tricky but it looks like it could be

00:08:46.399 --> 00:08:47.399
Nigeria.

00:08:47.399 --> 00:08:53.860
I’d better point out that we have discounted
mosquitos and tsetse flies as killers here,

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:58.579
since although they do spread a huge amount
of deadly disease; they themselves are not

00:08:58.579 --> 00:09:00.300
the actual killers.

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:04.519
So that leaves us with our next most lethal
group; snakes.

00:09:04.519 --> 00:09:09.510
Part of the problem is that in many countries,
people don’t head to hospital after being

00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:15.529
bitten, choosing local healers instead, so
no data is collected.

00:09:15.529 --> 00:09:22.460
In Nigeria, under 10% of bitees, not sure
if that’s a word… go to hospital, possibly

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:29.250
accounting for its very high death rate from
snake bites of 14 people per 100,000.

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:34.510
To make matters worse, Nigeria has a shortage
of antivenom thanks to distribution issues,

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:38.529
costs, and a lack of good education in rural
areas.

00:09:38.529 --> 00:09:45.100
The anitvenoms are pretty effective, reducing
the mortality rate by 70-90%, so the government

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:48.370
are working on improving access across the
country.

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:53.250
If you escape the snake, there’s a long
line of other creatures waiting to step up.

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:57.680
And the largest is the water horse, or Hippopotamus.

00:09:57.680 --> 00:10:03.380
Hippos take out almost 3,000 people a year
globally, being very aggressive and highly

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:04.810
territorial.

00:10:04.810 --> 00:10:10.639
At least in Africa, people are aware of the
dangers, but they are part of a very peculiar

00:10:10.639 --> 00:10:12.740
story in South America.

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:17.670
The notorious Columbian drug dealer, Pablo
Escobar, imported a wide range of animals

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:22.180
for his zoo, which he made free to the public.

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:27.310
But when his empire crumbled, the animals
were turned loose and hippos have thrived

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:32.480
in their new environment, maturing much earlier
than their African counterparts.

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:36.730
The locals still see them as cute and friendly
but it’s all fun and games until one of

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:38.460
them bites your face off.

00:10:38.460 --> 00:10:40.210
A final word on biting.

00:10:40.210 --> 00:10:45.640
For any of you worried about shark attack,
here’s a reassuring thought, you’re statistically

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:49.410
much more likely to get bitten by Luis Suarez
than a shark.

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:52.070
Now we turn to matters of the heart.

00:10:52.070 --> 00:10:57.250
But put down the flowers, and definitely throw
away those fatty chocolates, because we’re

00:10:57.250 --> 00:11:00.010
talking about cardiovascular disease.

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:06.760
This is by far the world’s biggest killer,
with over 1 in 10 deaths being down to a bad

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:07.760
ticker.

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:10.699
And who leads the world as the land of the
broken hearted?

00:11:10.699 --> 00:11:14.290
It’s the ex-soviet nation of Turkmenistan.

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:18.760
The country sits on top of Iran, like a cat
wrapped around its shoulders, but where Iran

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:25.700
has a reasonable healthcare system, Turkmenistan
is down in the bottom 20% of the world, according

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:28.930
to a World Health Organisation report from
2000.

00:11:28.930 --> 00:11:32.910
So, it’s more of a Garfield than a Puss
in Boots.

00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:35.220
Poor diet is another contributing factor.

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:40.240
The Turkmen diet consists of dishes such as
Plov, a dish made with rice and often the

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:42.190
very fatty mutton.

00:11:42.190 --> 00:11:47.320
Then there are skewers of meats like mutton
and pork, called Shashlyk, as well as dumplings

00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:48.350
called Manti.

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:50.920
And to quench their thirst?

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:57.579
Then you want to grab a delicious glass of
Chal, a sour white sparkling beverage, made

00:11:57.579 --> 00:11:59.890
from fermented camel milk.

00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:04.160
Mmm, I think I’d rather have a heart attack.

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:09.079
So, do what you’re told, and eat up all
your vegetables, or you’ll get sent to your

00:12:09.079 --> 00:12:13.260
room, which isn’t exactly the worst punishment
in the world.

00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:20.180
One punishment that is thankfully disappearing,
although rather slowly, is the Death Penalty.

00:12:20.180 --> 00:12:27.420
Right now, 94 countries have a legal death
penalty, but only 37 actively execute people.

00:12:27.420 --> 00:12:35.680
Of these 37, two are in the Americas, 11 in
Africa, 23 in Asia, and only Belarus in Europe.

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:40.940
In most cases, the punishment is reserved
for violent crimes, terrorism, and drug trafficking.

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:47.850
But in a few select countries the penalty
also sadly applies for adultery, apostasy

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:51.640
(meaning to abandon your religion) and homosexuality.

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:57.220
It’s not common but there have been executions
for all of these within the last 5 years.

00:12:57.220 --> 00:13:01.600
Come on world, we’re better than that, aren’t
we?

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:09.230
Equatorial Guinea is currently the world leader
per capita, with 11.56 people executed per

00:13:09.230 --> 00:13:14.680
million, leading 3.70 per million in Iran,
in second place.

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:22.440
But it is definitely China who has the itchiest
trigger finger since their total each year

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:26.459
easily matches that of the rest of the world
combined.

00:13:26.459 --> 00:13:33.230
In the early 2000s, the number was up around
12,000 people a year but it has now come down

00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:35.019
to around 2000.

00:13:35.019 --> 00:13:38.660
The difference in attitude to capital punishment
is not a new thing.

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:44.639
The first country to remove it from their
law was Venezuela, all the way back in 1863.

00:13:44.639 --> 00:13:51.750
Since 1989, at least one country per year
has moved to abolish it, with Fiji and Suriname

00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:54.269
being the last two, in 2015.

00:13:54.269 --> 00:14:00.709
When it comes to last meals, a study in the
US showed that fried chicken was probably

00:14:00.709 --> 00:14:02.670
the most common request.

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:08.050
One man, Philip Workman, asked that his last
meal be a vegetarian pizza but rather than

00:14:08.050 --> 00:14:11.660
giving it to him, they should give it to a
homeless person.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:17.199
The prison declined his request but across
Tennessee, thousands of dollars of pizza were

00:14:17.199 --> 00:14:22.509
donated to shelters on his behalf by good-willed
individuals.

00:14:22.509 --> 00:14:26.660
Next up, well … more down actually, is falling.

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:32.690
It may be surprising to hear that falling
is the second most lethal accident after vehicle

00:14:32.690 --> 00:14:40.699
collisions and, one study has claimed, that
it accounts for a whopping 35% of all accident

00:14:40.699 --> 00:14:43.170
and emergency visits.

00:14:43.170 --> 00:14:48.279
Your average emergency doctor’s day is probably
a couple of heart attacks, a stroke, a kid

00:14:48.279 --> 00:14:53.639
who swallowed pen lid and then someone who
fell off a roof, horse, ladder, climbing frame

00:14:53.639 --> 00:14:54.680
or palm tree.

00:14:54.680 --> 00:14:58.440
If it’s the last one then it’s probably
Keith Richards, you don’t need to treat

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:00.630
him, he’s clearly invincible.

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:02.589
So who leads the way?

00:15:02.589 --> 00:15:06.970
Well in the red corner, soon to be the black
and blue corner probably, we have the Titan

00:15:06.970 --> 00:15:10.380
of Tumbles, the Prince of Plummeting…it’s
Zambia!

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:15.630
It’s very difficult to get exact data on
this but it seems like the southern African

00:15:15.630 --> 00:15:22.300
nation is the falling capital, with a death
rate of 46 per 100,000.

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:26.210
There’s a combination of factors here that
could be the reason behind this.

00:15:26.210 --> 00:15:31.041
Obviously, a lack of great medical facilities
will always increase the mortality rate, as

00:15:31.041 --> 00:15:33.540
we’ve seen with many of the other examples
today.

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:39.020
But maybe there is something about the geography
of Zambia that adds to it.

00:15:39.020 --> 00:15:44.470
It’s mostly a high plateau and there are
a series of hills, such as the Mafinga Hills

00:15:44.470 --> 00:15:50.300
that are difficult to cross by car so you’ll
get more people climbing on foot through difficult

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:51.300
terrain.

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:57.170
It’s also home to one of the seven natural
wonders of the world; Victoria Falls.

00:15:57.170 --> 00:16:03.060
And fall you will, on occasion, if you are
one of the few brave tourists to take a dip

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:05.579
in the world’s most dangerous pool.

00:16:05.579 --> 00:16:11.410
Devil’s pool is a natural dell in the rock
that occurs right on the very lip of the tumbling

00:16:11.410 --> 00:16:12.410
water.

00:16:12.410 --> 00:16:16.500
Around August to January, the flow of the
river is quiet enough so that the natural

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:21.370
rock edge of the pool will keep you from being
hurled over the waterfall.

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:27.019
But, accidents have been known to happen so
obey the rules of the pool; that’s no bombing,

00:16:27.019 --> 00:16:29.260
no running and no heavy petting.

00:16:29.260 --> 00:16:33.949
Strangely, as dangerous as it looks, you’re
more likely to be one of the many people who

00:16:33.949 --> 00:16:40.319
die each year, falling out of bed – around
500 annually in the US alone.

00:16:40.319 --> 00:16:46.210
Turns out that falling dream is pretty
We turn now to a very small country in the

00:16:46.210 --> 00:16:51.110
Himalayan Mountains, with a population of
just over 700,000.

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:53.490
It is the beautiful kingdom of Bhutan.

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:59.860
It’s not easy to visit, they strictly control
tourist numbers and there is a daily fee of

00:16:59.860 --> 00:17:05.860
$250 that you have to pay, although it includes
your trips and hotel.

00:17:05.860 --> 00:17:09.900
So what is the killer here, I bet you are
wondering; exhaustion from all the climbing?

00:17:09.900 --> 00:17:12.010
Some kind of goat attack?

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:13.490
The answer is actually…

00:17:13.490 --> 00:17:14.490
poisoning.

00:17:14.490 --> 00:17:21.370
At 36 per 100,000, it is some way ahead of
the rest of the world, since everyone else

00:17:21.370 --> 00:17:24.970
except New Guinea is under 10 per 100,000.

00:17:24.970 --> 00:17:31.130
Due to a lack of regulation, Bhutan has allowed
a high quantity of heavy metals, such as chromium

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:36.970
and manganese, to simply be flushed into the
local water supply after experiments and so

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:37.970
on.

00:17:37.970 --> 00:17:44.250
This is especially odd as the country is famous
for being one of the world’s leading environmentally

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:45.559
focused places.

00:17:45.559 --> 00:17:50.491
I guess they never thought of it as a problem,
whereas in many industrial nations, there

00:17:50.491 --> 00:17:53.640
is a long history of poisonings to look back
at.

00:17:53.640 --> 00:18:00.299
Chromium, for example, was famously what contaminated
the town of Hinkley, California, and caused

00:18:00.299 --> 00:18:06.260
noticeably higher rates of cancer, covered
in the Julia Roberts film Erin Brockovich.

00:18:06.260 --> 00:18:11.620
More recently, the lead poisonings in Flint,
Michigan, show that we never know when the

00:18:11.620 --> 00:18:13.740
water might go bad.

00:18:13.740 --> 00:18:18.059
It was actually a lead poisoning that put
Bhutan in the news a few years back.

00:18:18.059 --> 00:18:23.980
A man in Switzerland was diagnosed with heavy
metal poisoning and they found that on his

00:18:23.980 --> 00:18:29.559
frequent trips to Bhutan, he had been taking
an alternative medicine and the pills were

00:18:29.559 --> 00:18:32.920
covered in a red paint, high in lead.

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:37.730
The man was hoping to cure his condition of
Bell’s palsy, a type of face paralysis.

00:18:37.730 --> 00:18:43.320
He was told the pills contained the hair of
a dead Bhutanese priest but when they were

00:18:43.320 --> 00:18:45.549
analysed, no trace was found.

00:18:45.549 --> 00:18:50.460
I personally, prefer my medicine without a
dead man’s fringe in it, but each to their

00:18:50.460 --> 00:18:51.520
own, I guess.

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:57.160
And finally, one of the most First World Problems
I’ve ever come across.

00:18:57.160 --> 00:19:02.520
The USA leads the planet for a truly heroic
way to go.

00:19:02.520 --> 00:19:07.500
Averaging two embarrassing funerals per year,
it’s the country where you are most likely

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:09.679
to be crushed to death by a vending machine.

00:19:09.679 --> 00:19:13.270
At least there’ll be plenty of snacks at
the wake.

00:19:13.270 --> 00:19:19.620
So, the world might be a dangerous place sometimes
but let’s not all get too paranoid.

00:19:19.620 --> 00:19:24.040
Life expectancy keeps on creeping up and you’ll
probably end up living far longer than you

00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:25.740
wanted to anyway.

00:19:25.740 --> 00:19:29.440
You might still be around for series 49 of
Games of Thrones.

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:34.100
For those of you that have managed to stay
alive all the way through this video, well

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:58.030
done and thanks for the view, subscribe for
more Thoughty2.

